<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liu Heita</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 623</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liu Heita (died 623) was a general of the rebel leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dou-jiande">Dou Jiande</a> in the wars after the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui dynasty</a>. After the Tang captured and executed Dou in 621, his former officers rose under Liu Heita, who quickly recovered Dou's lands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebei">Hebei</a> and proclaimed himself Prince of Handong. Tang armies under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang">Li Shimin</a> and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-jiancheng">Li Jiancheng</a> defeated him, and he was betrayed and executed early in 623.</p></div>
